    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "Raleigh ist die Hauptstadt von North Carolina und Teil des Research Triangle, einer der am schnellsten wachsenden Technologieregionen der USA. Die Stadt wurde 1792 als neuer Regierungssitz gegründet und nach Sir Walter Raleigh benannt. Raleigh beherbergt die North Carolina State University sowie Forschungseinrichtungen wie das Research Triangle Park. Die Wirtschaft wird durch Technologie, Bildung, Gesundheitswesen und Biotechnologie angetrieben. Die Stadt hat eine lebendige Kulturszene mit dem North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences, dem North Carolina Museum of Art und dem Duke Energy Center for the Performing Arts.",
      hu: "Raleigh Észak-Karolina fővárosa, a Research Triangle régió része, amely az Egyesült Államok egyik vezető technológiai központja. A várost 1792-ben alapították kifejezetten fővárosnak, és Walter Raleigh-ről nevezték el. Itt található az Észak-Karolinai Állami Egyetem, valamint a Research Triangle Park, amely több mint 300 vállalatnak ad otthont. A gazdaságot a technológia, az oktatás, az egészségügy és a biotechnológia jellemzi. A város kulturális élete gazdag, számos múzeummal, színházzal és fesztivállal.",
      ro: "Raleigh este capitala statului Carolina de Nord, situat în regiunea Research Triangle, un pol major de tehnologie și cercetare. Orașul a fost fondat în 1792 ca nouă capitală, numit după Sir Walter Raleigh. Raleigh găzduiește Universitatea de Stat din Carolina de Nord și Research Triangle Park, care include sedii ale companii precum IBM, Cisco și GlaxoSmithKline. Economia este bazată pe tehnologia informației, biotehnologie, educație și servicii medicale. Muzeul de Științe Naturale și Muzeul de Artă sunt principalele atracții culturale. Orașul se numără printre cele mai rapide creșteri demografice din SUA.",
      en: "Raleigh is the capital of North Carolina and the second-largest city in the state. Founded in 1792 as the capital, it was named after Sir Walter Raleigh. The city is a key component of the Research Triangle region, anchored by the Research Triangle Park (RTP), which houses over 300 companies including IBM, Cisco, and BASF. Raleigh is home to North Carolina State University, a major public research university. The economy is driven by technology, life sciences, education, and healthcare. The city has a high quality of life, with extensive greenways, parks, and a growing food scene. Raleigh's population has grown by over 20% since 2010, making it one of the fastest-growing major cities in the US.",
    },
